  "paper_id": "sigcomm-2025-splidt-partitioned-decision-trees-for-scalable-stateful-1fca9b1e",
  "title": "SpliDT: Partitioned Decision Trees for Scalable Stateful Inference at Line Rate",
  "abstract": "Machine learning is increasingly used in programmable data planes, such as switches [4, 12, 13] and smartNICs [1, 16], to enable real-time traffic analysis and security monitoring at line rate. Decision trees (DTs) are particularly well-suited for these tasks due to their interpretability and compatibility with the Reconfigurable Match-Action Table (RMT) architecture. However, current DT implementations require collecting all features upfront, which limits scalability and accuracy due to constrained data plane resources.",
